<div class="step-strip"><span><strong>1</strong> Choose N, k and a mass profile</span><span><strong>2</strong> Run or step the experiment</span><span><strong>3</strong> Read the plots and export the run</span><a href="Guide.html">Full operating guide</a></div>
<div class="quick-cases" id="quickCases"><button id="caseBlind">Blind-mode probe: N=24, k=6</button><button id="caseCoprime">Coprime: N=25, k=6</button><button id="caseComplement">Repeat with complementary control</button><a href="Structure_Comparison.html#arithmetic">Large-N arithmetic study</a></div>
<div class="lab-workspace"><aside class="setup-panel"><h2>Experiment setup</h2><div class="setup-pair"><div><label for="labN">Robots N</label><input id="labN" type="number" min="3" max="80" value="24"></div><div><label for="labK">Service order k</label><input id="labK" type="number" min="1" max="80" value="6"></div></div><p id="parameterPreview"></p>
<label for="labProfile">Initial sector masses</label><select id="labProfile"><option value="unequal">Seeded unequal masses</option><option value="equal">Equal masses</option><option value="blind">Pure service-blind harmonic</option><option value="visible">Observable harmonic</option></select><div id="singlePolicySetup"><label for="labPolicy">Boundary controller</label><select id="labPolicy"><option value="single">Service order k only</option><option value="complement">k + adjacent order</option><option value="switch">Persistent switching</option></select></div>
<div class="fault-only" id="faultSetup"><label for="faultPolicies">Policies shown together</label><select id="faultPolicies"><option value="two">Single + complementary</option><option value="three">Add persistent switching</option></select><div class="setup-pair"><div><label for="labFaultTime">Removal time (s)</label><input id="labFaultTime" type="number" min="0" max="200" value="8"></div><div><label for="labFailed">Failed physical ID</label><input id="labFailed" type="number" min="1" max="80" value="13"></div></div><p>Click a robot in the map to choose its physical ID before starting the new trial.</p></div>
<div class="lab-buttons"><button id="labRun" class="primary">Run experiment</button><button id="labStep">One step</button></div><div class="lab-buttons"><button id="labReset">Apply / reset</button><button id="labRandom">New random start</button></div><label for="positionSeed">Position seed</label><input id="positionSeed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="2718"><p>Random feasible positions are the default. Reusing the same seed reproduces the same initial robots.</p>
<details><summary>Map, timing and display</summary><label for="labRegion">Planar free-space domain</label><select id="labRegion"><option value="none">Unit disk</option><option value="three">Disk with 3 circular holes</option><option value="five">Disk with 5 circular holes</option></select><label for="labDensity">Demand density</label><select id="labDensity"><option value="hotspots">Two demand hotspots</option><option value="uniform">Uniform</option></select><label for="labPlacement">Robot initialization</label><select id="labPlacement"><option value="random">Random feasible positions</option><option value="ring">Seeded perturbed ring</option></select><label for="massSeed">Unequal-mass seed</label><input id="massSeed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="2718"><label for="labDuration">Motion duration (s)</label><input id="labDuration" type="number" min="1" max="200" value="24"><label for="labSelected">Selected physical ID</label><input id="labSelected" type="number" min="1" max="80" value="1"><label for="labSpeed">Steps per display frame</label><select id="labSpeed"><option>1</option><option>3</option><option>8</option></select><label for="labScale">Error / energy plot scale</label><select id="labScale"><option value="log">Logarithmic</option><option value="linear">Linear</option></select></details><p>Single-integrator robots, 0.2 s updates, speed bound 0.45, exact swept circular-clearance checks. Full reliable snapshots and a known map.</p><a href="Guide.html#metric-dictionary">What do the metrics mean?</a></aside>
<div class="dashboard-area"><div id="labMessage" class="trial-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="faultBanner" class="event-banner fault-only"></div><div id="labMetrics" class="metric-cards"></div><div class="replay-strip" id="replayStrip"><strong>Recorded timeline</strong><input id="labTimeline" type="range" min="0" max="0" value="0"><span id="timelineLabel">Initial state</span><button id="beforeFault" class="fault-only">Before removal</button><button id="afterFault" class="fault-only">After removal</button><button id="liveEnd">Latest state</button></div><div id="labMaps" class="map-grid"></div>
<div class="dashboard-charts" id="labPerformance"><section class="plot"><h2>Responsibility-load imbalance</h2><canvas id="labLoadPlot" role="img" aria-label="Relative responsibility load error by motion time"></canvas><p>RMS(ell - k/N) / (k/N). Zero means equal responsibility workload. Each curve is one boundary-control policy.</p></section><section class="plot"><h2>Actual robot control input</h2><canvas id="labInputPlot" role="img" aria-label="Applied robot velocity RMS by motion time"></canvas><p>RMS norm of the applied velocity after safety projection and step scaling, in domain units/s. Small input alone does not prove load balance.</p></section><section class="plot"><h2>Basic-mass and blind energies</h2><canvas id="labEnergyPlot" role="img" aria-label="Basic mass and blind projection coordination energies"></canvas><p>E_mass = massError squared / 2; E_blind = blindError squared / 2. Their difference is observable basic-mass energy. These are coordination costs, not mechanical energy.</p></section><section class="plot"><h2>Geometric coverage cost H</h2><canvas id="labCostPlot" role="img" aria-label="Assigned Euclidean coverage cost and centroid lower bound"></canvas><p>H = integral of the assigned squared-distance sum / (2k). Dashed: unconstrained centroid lower bound for the first policy. Changing rays or removing a robot can raise H.</p></section><section class="plot"><h2>Selected robot: applied u_x and u_y</h2><canvas id="labVectorPlot" role="img" aria-label="Selected physical robot Cartesian velocity components"></canvas><p id="selectedInputNote">First policy. Actual commands in domain units/s, not the unsafeguarded centroid request.</p></section><section class="plot"><h2>Virtual-boundary control input</h2><canvas id="labBoundaryPlot" role="img" aria-label="Cumulative mass coordinate boundary velocity RMS"></canvas><p>RMS dx_i/dt, in mass fraction/s. The ray is theta_i = F inverse(x_i); its input is distinct from robot velocity.</p></section><section class="plot"><h2>Current sector masses and service loads</h2><canvas id="labMassPlot" role="img" aria-label="Normalized masses and loads by current cyclic role"></canvas><p>First policy: blue N*m_i, orange N*ell_i/k; ideal value 1. Physical IDs remain attached to robots after removal.</p></section><section class="plot"><h2>Fourier response of the responsibility rule</h2><canvas id="labSpectrumPlot" role="img" aria-label="Normalized squared Fourier gain and exact cyclic blind frequencies"></canvas><p>G_j = squared magnitude of R_k(j)/k. Exact zeros count gcd(N,k)-1 nonconstant blind modes. This operator plot is separate from robot motion.</p></section></div>
<div class="lab-buttons"><button id="labJson">Download run JSON</button><button id="labCsv">Download metrics CSV</button><button id="labPng">Download performance PNG</button><button id="labShare">Copy settings link</button></div><p id="labObservation" class="muted"></p><details><summary>Metric dictionary and interpretation</summary><div id="labDictionary" class="metric-dictionary"></div><p><a href="cost-theory.html">Gcd-sensitive coordination objectives and proofs</a> · <a href="Guide.html">Rigorous operating guide</a></p></details><details class="fault-only"><summary>Announced-removal event records</summary><pre id="labEvents"></pre></details></div></div>
